# Discovery over CAN (docs/can_support.md, pin inventory): LinuxCNC's end
# (linuxcnc/stmblcan's stmblcan_bus_discover, on the simulated MCP2515) asks
# the simulated drive's can component for its description, then runs with
# it: the drive's vel_scale (set to 250 in its config here) comes from the
# drive. An absent node gets no answer.
@args --drive tests/can/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
can0.vel_scale = 250
run 0.1
lcnccan discover 7
lcnccan discover 1
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 31.4
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
canstat
@match ^lcnccan: node 7: no answer$
@match ^lcnccan: node 1 describes itself:$
@match ^device stbl$
@match ^profile stmbl1$
@match ^vel_scale 250$
@match ^lcnccan: node 1, vel_scale 250, 1 Mbit/s$
@expect hv0.sim_vel ~ 19.73 1%
@match ^can: present 1 fb [0-9]+ missed 0 tx_late 0
